Impact Analysis: Removing Azure APIM from Current Architecture
Current Workflow

User → Cloudflare → Firewall → Azure APIM → AKS Internal LB (Ingress) → Istio Ingress → Pod

What Happens If We Remove Azure APIM?
New Workflow

User → Cloudflare → Firewall → AKS Internal LB (Ingress) → Istio Ingress → Pod

Context

APIs are publicly exposed

All traffic already enters through Cloudflare

AKS uses Istio for internal traffic control

APIM currently performs path rewriting

Path Handling (Important Migration Consideration)
Current Behavior via APIM

Example:

External URL:
marketdata.xyz.com/md/health

APIM:

Exposes /md/* publicly

Strips /md

Forwards internally as:

marketdata.xyz.com/health

So APIM currently performs path-based abstraction and rewriting.

Migration Plan (Without APIM)

Before removing APIM:

Configure Istio Ingress Gateway to accept the same public paths (/md/*)

Implement path rewrite rules in Istio (or Cloudflare if preferred)

Ensure backend services continue receiving:

/health instead of /md/health

This guarantees:

No endpoint changes for external consumers

No breaking changes

Seamless transition

