Benefits of Removing APIM

Reduced latency (one hop removed)

Reduced Azure cost

Simpler architecture

Fewer moving parts

Security remains enforced at Cloudflare edge

Istio already provides internal traffic management

Path rewrite can be replicated in Istio

Risks

Public API governance shifts away from Azure

Consumer onboarding must be handled externally

Subscription-based access control must move to:

Application layer

Cloudflare Workers

Loss of built-in developer portal

Executive Summary

For security, routing, caching, and path management, Cloudflare + Istio fully replace APIM capabilities.

For public API governance, subscription management, developer portal, and structured API lifecycle control, APIM still provides additional value.

Removing APIM is technically feasible without breaking existing URLs (via Istio path alignment), but the decision should depend on how much you rely on API consumer governance versus pure edge security.
